I have two requests:
- Please print alternate platform name in event log, now it is not obvious if BOINC client started using value configured in cc_config.xml using `<alt_platform>` or not;
- I have Odroid C2 which uses platform `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, and I have tag `<alt_platform>arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf</alt_platform>` in my cc_config.xml. Now I would like to add second alternative platform `<alt_platform>armv6l-unknown-linux-gnueabihf</alt_platform>`. [Client configuration](https://boinc.berkeley.edu/wiki/Client_configuration) page does not say if it is possible to use this tag multiple times, so I assume that this would not work (I did not try to to this). Please either add such feature to BOINC or update that page.

